# FloodWatch AI V2/V3 - Verification and Walkthrough

## Summary of Accomplishments

I have successfully upgraded the **FloodWatch AI MVP** to **V3**, transforming the standard dashboard into a true **Multi-Agent AI Pipeline**. The core engine was completely refactored to orchestrate distinct AI personas that transparently monitor, verify, decide, and publish sequentially.

### 1. Multi-Agent AI Architecture
The [MockDataService](file:///Users/nileshtailor/Hackathon/MacroHard/floodwatch-ai/src/services/MockDataService.ts#14-224) no longer houses monolithic inline arrays. Instead, it asynchronously orchestrates 5 isolated agents:
- **Vision Agent**: Evaluates simulated webcam bounding boxes. If standing water is verified, it emits a HIGH confidence signal and a semantic reasoning trace.
- **Sensor Fusion Agent**: Merges physical sewer telemetry, weather alerts, and real-time traffic speeds mathematically to compute zone-level `riskScores` and textual explanations.
- **Verification Agent**: The validator. It intercepts `UNVERIFIED` incidents and enforces Source Consensus Logic. Only upon finding 2 HIGH sources (or 1 HIGH/1 MEDIUM) does it legally upgrade the incident to `VERIFIED`.
- **Decision Agent**: Evaluates the `VERIFIED` state and maps it to specific operational intents, generating context-aware `RecommendedActions` (e.g. "Issue Immediate Citizen Alert" or "Dispatch Heavy Barricades").
- **Publishing Agent**: Acts as the outbound API formatter. Generates `CitizenAlerts` and compiles the physical Claim Evidence Log `data` payloads.

### 2. LLM Provider Abstraction
To future-proof the application for Nemotron/Gemini, an [LLMProvider](file:///Users/nileshtailor/Hackathon/MacroHard/floodwatch-ai/src/lib/llm-provider.ts#8-29) ([src/lib/llm-provider.ts](file:///Users/nileshtailor/Hackathon/MacroHard/floodwatch-ai/src/lib/llm-provider.ts)) was implemented. Currently, it acts as a deterministic fallback—combining strings predictably so the app runs instantaneously without API keys—but all Decision and Publishing agents await its asynchronous generation outputs, making the backend completely ready for an LLM client drop-in.

### 3. State Engine UI & The "AI Reasoning Trace"
- The [AgentTrace](file:///Users/nileshtailor/Hackathon/MacroHard/floodwatch-ai/src/types/schemas.ts#53-61) interface strictly types every AI operation (`{ agentName, inputContext, outputSummary, reasoning, timestamp }`).
- The **Incident Detail Panel** has been upgraded with a tabbed interface. Toggling to the **AI Reasoning Trace** tab allows users to visually audit the pipeline in chronological order, displaying exactly what each Agent saw, how it reasoned over the data, and its final conclusion. 
- The map and base SSE streaming mechanisms remain intact, elegantly visualizing the agent outputs in real-time.

